# Live-verified against the real container 2026-10-04, after a golden-image
# review caught that this file's TOUCH taps originally used the default
# hold_s (0.6s), which EXCEEDS this widget's own long-press threshold
# (`HOLD_MS` 350ms, multitap_keyboard_window.c): a 0.6s touch on a nav
# arrow key isn't read as a single tap at all - it's long enough to fire
# the SAME hold-to-repeat timer the on-screen DEL key uses
# (`multitap_keyboard_delete_repeat_ms`), so "two taps" moved the cursor
# much further than 2 characters (all the way to the start, in practice),
# and the follow-up "type a letter" touch registered as a long-press
# digit-insert instead of a tap (see keyboard_long_press_digit_insert.seq's
# own header for that mechanism). Every tap below now passes an explicit
# 0.1s hold (comfortably under 350ms).
#
# Confirmed live: DOWN cycles the plain label keyboard through ALPHA ->
# NUMBERS -> SYMBOLS -> NAV (3 presses from the default ALPHA page reaches
# NAV - `Page` enum order in multitap_keyboard.c), the NAV page shows
# left/right arrow keys at the SAME grid positions pattern/numeric mode's
# own key 3/5 occupy (row 1, col 0 and col 2 - cx 33/165, cy 113 on this
# platform's 200x228 display), and BACK cancels the whole keyboard from
# ANY page, not just ALPHA (confirmed: BACK on the NAV page reverted the
# label to its original text, same as BACK on the default page).
#
# Keys: TestClearAlarms=10008, TestAlarmIndex=10009, TestAlarmHour=10010,
# TestAlarmMinute=10011, TestAlarmName=10020
IMPORT ../common/wipe_and_prep.seq
APPMSG --int 10008=1 10009=0 10010=7 10011=0 --string 10020=Wakeup
SLEEP 1

TAP down
LONGPRESS select
SLEEP 1
TAP down
TAP down
SLEEP 1
TAP select
# Let the keyboard caret rest solid-on (CARET_IDLE_MS) before capturing.
SLEEP 5
# The keyboard's text cursor blinks until the keyboard has been idle ~5s, then stops:
# wait that out so the screenshot never lands on a different blink phase.
SLEEP 5
SCREENSHOT label_keyboard_alpha_page_prefilled

TAP down
SLEEP 1
# The keyboard's text cursor blinks until the keyboard has been idle ~5s, then stops:
# wait that out so the screenshot never lands on a different blink phase.
SLEEP 5
SCREENSHOT label_keyboard_numbers_page
TAP down
SLEEP 1
# The keyboard's text cursor blinks until the keyboard has been idle ~5s, then stops:
# wait that out so the screenshot never lands on a different blink phase.
SLEEP 5
SCREENSHOT label_keyboard_symbols_page
TAP down
SLEEP 1
# The keyboard's text cursor blinks until the keyboard has been idle ~5s, then stops:
# wait that out so the screenshot never lands on a different blink phase.
SLEEP 5
SCREENSHOT label_keyboard_nav_page_arrow_keys

# Move the cursor left 2 characters (from after "Wakeup" to between "ak"
# and "eup"), then type "A" at that position.
TOUCH 33 113 0.1
SLEEP 1
TOUCH 33 113 0.1
SLEEP 1
# Let the keyboard caret rest solid-on (CARET_IDLE_MS) before capturing.
SLEEP 5
# The keyboard's text cursor blinks until the keyboard has been idle ~5s, then stops:
# wait that out so the screenshot never lands on a different blink phase.
SLEEP 5
SCREENSHOT cursor_moved_left_2
TAP down
SLEEP 1
TOUCH 99 68 0.1
SLEEP 1
# Let the keyboard caret rest solid-on (CARET_IDLE_MS) before capturing.
SLEEP 5
# The keyboard's text cursor blinks until the keyboard has been idle ~5s, then stops:
# wait that out so the screenshot never lands on a different blink phase.
SLEEP 5
SCREENSHOT a_inserted_mid_string
TAP select
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT edit_menu_label_with_inserted_char --mask-rect 70x25+0+203
